      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, one pill is one pill too many. Lisinopril already holds onto potassium like a miser holds gold—adding more is a one-way ticket to a cardiac arrest. The salt in tonic water works because it pulls water into your muscles and calms the nerve endings that are misfiring. And the quinine in the tonic water is a proven cramp-killer, not some fairy tale. So skip the pills, grab a cold glass of tonic, and thank me when your legs stop screaming at 3 a.m.",
